lternatively record as string \"110–165 / 130–195 / 190–225\" with unit mm. Hmm. The ranges are three length ranges for the different sizes. I think config_level with axis \"connection size\" mapping in order is a reasonable, likely-intended interpretation... but it is an inference. Safer: record type_level \"installed_length_brass_body\" as value string \"110–165 / 130–195 / 190–225\", unit mm. I'll do the string form to avoid fabricating the mapping. Actually, let me do config_level with condition \"varies by connection size\" — no, that's not a condition. I'll go with the string.\n\nHmm, but rule 2 says ranges become {min,max}. Three ranges in one cell is a list. As a string \"110–165 / 130–195 / 190–225\" it stays faithful. I'll keep string with unit_symbol \"mm\".\n\n- eut_testing_category: \"Ultrasonic water meter\", eut_case: \"B\" (OIML R 49-2:2013, 8.1.8). Record as type_level: eut_category \"Ultrasonic water meter\", eut_case \"B\". Maybe skip — it's about testing per R49-2. I'll include \"eut_test_case\": \"B\" with maybe note. I'll include it.\n\n- Q2/Q1 = 1.6, Q4/Q3 = 1.25 as type_level.\n- Q3/Q1 ratios: covered per model.\n- Nominal diameters: 15, 20, 25 mm → model-level.\n\nNow certificate-level: The fragment includes certificate number R49/2013-A-CZ1-26.03, issuing authority Český metrologický institut (Czech Metrology Institute), page count 9. Should I fill certificate? The instruction: \"Return a JSON object conforming to the layered schema for the content present in THIS fragment only. Omit sections that are not present in this fragment.\"\n\nThe certificate number IS present in this fragment (mentioned repeatedly: R49/2013-A-CZ1-26.03). Page total 9 present. Scheme: the number format \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-26.03\" — \"A\" indicates scheme A. Hmm, in OIML-CS, certificate numbers like \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-26.03\" — the \"-A-\" after year denotes scheme A. I think scheme \"A\" is right. The issuing authority: Český metrologický institut (Czech Metrology Insti