  \"family_name\": \"WMP\",\n    \"models\": [ 15 entries ]\n  },\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {...},\n    \"model_level\": [...],\n    \"config_level\": []  // maybe omit if not used\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [...],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R49\",\n    \"edition\": 2013,\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [\"2\"]\n  }\n}\n\nconfig_level: I decided pressure_loss_class as type-level string. So no config_level. Or should I use config_level for the length ranges? Length ranges by connection size — mapping inference. Keep string. So omit config_level entirely.\n\nWait, reconsider pressure_loss_class once more. \"ΔP40 (ΔP63 for one variant)\". As type_level single value: \"ΔP40 (ΔP63 for one variant)\". Acceptable.\n\nType-level characteristics list:\n\n- measuring_principle: {\"value\": \"Ultrasonic\"}\n- accuracy_class: {\"value\": 2} — number, dimensionless. Or \"2\"? Class 2 numeric fine.\n- temperature_class: {\"value\": \"T30 or T50\"}\n- maximum_admissible_temperature: {\"value\": 50, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n- maximum_admissible_pressure: {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"}\n- water_pressure_class: {\"value\": \"MAP16\"}\n- pressure_loss_class: {\"value\": \"ΔP40 (ΔP63 for one variant)\"}\n- reverse_flow: {\"value\": \"Not designed to measure\"}\n- environmental_class: {\"value\": \"O\"}\n- environmental_class_temperature_range: {\"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 70}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n- electromagnetic_environment_class: {\"value\": \"E1\"}\n- mechanical_environment_class: {\"value\": \"M1\"}\n- protection_degree: {\"value\": \"IP68\"}\n- orientation: {\"value\": \"vertical, flow from top to bottom (V↓)\"}\n- indicating_range: {\"value\": 99999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"}\n- indicating_device_resolution: {\"value\": 0.000001, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"}\n- q2_q1_ratio: {\"value\": 1.6}\n- q4_q3_ratio: {\"value\": 1.25}\n- power_supply_type: {\"value\": \"Non-replaceable battery\"}\n- battery_voltage_